      "rows": [
        [
          "Why were spices expensive pre-1800?",
          "Geographic monopoly + multiple middlemen + no refrigeration + medicinal value"
        ],
        [
          "What broke the spice monopolies?",
          "Portuguese Cape route (1498) → VOC by force → transplantation breaks geographic lock (1770s)"
        ],
        [
          "What family dominates \"warming\" spices?",
          "Zingiberaceae: ginger, turmeric, cardamom, galangal"
        ],
        [
          "What creates heat vs aroma?",
          "Heat = TRPV1/TRPA1 pain receptors; aroma = olfactory receptors"
        ],
        [
          "What were the most valuable spices by weight?",
          "Saffron (still is), then pepper/cloves/nutmeg/vanilla historically"
        ],
        [
          "What compound class explains \"anise\" flavor in unrelated plants?",
          "Anethole (phenylpropanoid) — convergent synthesis in anise, fennel, star anise"
        ],
        [
          "Why did chilies spread so fast after 1492?",
          "Easy to grow tropics-wide, shelf-stable, vitamin C source, replaced expensive pepper"
        ],
        [
          "What financed the Dutch Golden Age?",
          "VOC nutmeg monopoly, enforced by genocide in the Banda Islands"
        ]
